WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.484 --> 00:00:02.547
...I heard

00:00:02.636 --> 00:00:04.321
Water Imps have a special elixir...

00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:05.981
I know...

00:00:06.059 --> 00:00:08.084
Could that be the secret

00:00:08.496 --> 00:00:09.371
Behind the Prima Donna's voice...?

00:00:09.681 --> 00:00:11.356
Wait, shhh...!

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.787
If only I could sing like the Prima Donna

00:00:17.071 --> 00:00:19.237
I'd do anything. Whatever it takes...

00:00:19.581 --> 00:00:22.800
Whatever it takes...?

00:00:23.538 --> 00:00:24.290
Prima Donna!?

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.593
...I'm sorry, Prima Donna!

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.203
I just—

00:00:32.275 --> 00:00:33.931
Want to be a singer?

00:00:35.784 --> 00:00:36.515
Yes...

00:00:36.927 --> 00:00:37.915
Why?

00:00:38.318 --> 00:00:39.859
The troupe is the only place

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.581
...I won't go hungry

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:45.877
I know it's a selfish reason, but I...

00:00:45.877 --> 00:00:46.618
No

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:49.221
I actually find it quite admirable

00:00:50.468 --> 00:00:53.387
Here, this will help your voice

00:00:53.905 --> 00:00:54.988
But first

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.309
Tell me

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:59.165
What do you want your voice to sound like?

00:00:59.421 --> 00:01:00.787
Sound like...?

00:01:01.315 --> 00:01:02.331
Perhaps...

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:03.668
As soft

00:01:03.671 --> 00:01:04.868
Gentle

00:01:05.143 --> 00:01:07.862
And sweet as a childhood dream

00:01:08.606 --> 00:01:11.575
Or passionate and brilliant

00:01:11.696 --> 00:01:14.203
A voice capable of commanding center stage

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.650
Or perhaps something colder

00:01:19.196 --> 00:01:22.196
That feeling of farewell or a final curtain call

00:01:23.278 --> 00:01:24.053
Then...

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.178
Which one would you choose? Which kind of voice?

00:01:29.368 --> 00:01:32.621
I wouldn't choose any single "one"

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:56.913
My voice drifts between a multitude of possibilities, wandering to and fro...

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.352
...Endlessly searching for a path that leads toward home

00:02:04.485 --> 00:02:05.509
I'm sorry, Prima Donna

00:02:06.217 --> 00:02:09.223
But I... I still don't understand...

00:02:09.236 --> 00:02:10.052
Heh

00:02:10.052 --> 00:02:11.912
Long to be someone else

00:02:11.912 --> 00:02:14.641
And you're bound to forget your own voice

00:02:14.699 --> 00:02:16.818
But I like the answer you gave

00:02:16.879 --> 00:02:17.974
The way I see it...

00:02:18.096 --> 00:02:21.809
You're more in tune with your heart than most

00:02:23.026 --> 00:02:23.939
So...

00:02:24.347 --> 00:02:25.930
...Take this lozenge

00:02:26.136 --> 00:02:27.814
And we can start practicing in a bit

00:02:27.871 --> 00:02:29.435
...Huh? Lozen—

00:02:29.435 --> 00:02:30.352
Prima Donna!? 

00:02:30.352 --> 00:02:31.214
—Mmph... —Hahaha

00:02:31.214 --> 00:02:34.557
After that, go practice another run of high notes...

00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:36.620
Ah, no, make it three

00:02:37.098 --> 00:02:38.096
Oh

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:41.664
And no more talk of this "elixir" for now

00:02:41.974 --> 00:02:44.754
*sigh* That was the last of my lozenges

